    ============================================================================
    PROMO / ANNOUNCEMENT SYSTEM — p_struct.html
    ============================================================================

    WHAT WAS ADDED:
    Two promotional UI elements added directly to the base template (p_struct.html)
    so they are inherited by EVERY page in the AbhiHub Premium app automatically.

    ============================================================================
    1. TOP ANNOUNCEMENT STRIP  (#promoStrip)
    ============================================================================
    - Fixed to the very top of the viewport (z-index: 8500)
    - Background: linear-gradient(90deg, #7c3aed → #2563eb → #06b6d4)
    - Contains:
        • A pill badge  → class="promo-tag"     (e.g. "✨ New")
        • Message text  → id="promoStripText"
        • CTA link      → id="promoStripLink"   (yellow color #ffe769)
        • Dismiss btn   → id="promoStripClose"  (calls dismissPromoStrip())
    - Animates in with promoSlideDown keyframe (0.45s)
    - Hides with class="hidden" (slides top: -60px)
    - Pushes body paddingTop so content isn't overlapped

    localStorage key : 'abhihub_promo_strip_dismissed'
    Version string   : PROMO_VER = 'v2'  ← bump to re-show after an update

    ============================================================================
    2. PROMO CARD MODAL  (#promoCardOverlay / #promoCard)
    ============================================================================
    - Full-screen overlay with backdrop-filter: blur(4px), z-index: 9200
    - Card appears with fade + slide-up animation
    - Auto-shows after 4000ms on page load (only if not dismissed)
    - Structure:
        • .promo-card-header  — gradient header with bouncing emoji + title + subtitle
        • .promo-features-list — icon chips (violet/blue/teal/amber) + feature text
        • .promo-cta-btn      — gradient CTA button (links to /features by default)
        • .promo-dismiss-link — "Maybe later" text link
    - Closes on: close button click / "Maybe later" / backdrop click

    localStorage key : 'abhihub_promo_card_dismissed'
    Version string   : PROMO_VER = 'v2'  ← same var, shared with strip

    ============================================================================
    3. JAVASCRIPT API  (window.showPromo)
    ============================================================================
    Call from ANY page's JS to trigger a custom promo without touching the template:

        window.showPromo({
            stripText    : 'Summer Sale — 50% off premium!',
            stripLink    : { href: '/sale', label: 'Claim offer →' },
            cardEmoji    : '🎉',
            cardTitle    : 'Limited-time offer',
            cardDesc     : 'Get premium at half the price',
            cardFeatures : [
                { icon: '💰', color: 'amber', text: '50% discount on all plans' },
                { icon: '📄', color: 'violet', text: 'Unlimited PDF downloads' }
            ],
            ctaLabel     : 'Grab the deal',
            ctaHref      : '/sale'
        });

    Available pf-icon colors: violet | blue | teal | amber

    ============================================================================
    4. CONTROL FUNCTIONS (global)
    ============================================================================
        dismissPromoStrip()   — hides strip + saves to localStorage permanently
        dismissPromoCard()    — hides card + saves to localStorage permanently
        closePromoCard()      — hides card without saving (re-shows next visit)
        showPromo(cfg)        — show a fully custom promo (see API above)

    ============================================================================
    5. HOW TO UPDATE / RE-SHOW PROMO
    ============================================================================
    In p_struct.html, inside the <!-- ===== PROMO LOGIC ===== --> script block,
    change the PROMO_VER constant:

        const PROMO_VER = 'v3';   // was 'v2' — users who dismissed v2 will see v3

    This invalidates any previously stored dismissal and shows the promo again.

